    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d797">

                <pb facs="1201" n="1185" xml:id="pg1185"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/6–2749</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Acting Secretary of
                            State to the President
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-27">June 27, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>There are attached herewith in accordance with your request of June 16, copies of
                    cables covering talks held between Mr. Mark Ethridge, United States
                    Representative on the Palestine Conciliation Commission, and Israeli Prime
                    Minister David Ben Gurion.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d797-f1"/>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d797-f1" n="1" xml:id="d797-f1-content">
                <p>The copies enclosed were telegrams from Jerusalem, as follows: Nos. 274, 275, and
                    277, April 9; 291, April 13; 308, April 19; and 312, April 20. All of these
                    messages are printed in this compilation, except for No. 308; regarding No. 308,
                    see footnote 1, <ref target="#pg923">p. 923</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
